<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mayombe</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mayombe is a region of low mountains and dense rainforest along the Atlantic coast of west-central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>, stretching across the Cabinda enclave of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angola">Angola</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-kongo">Kongo</a> Central province of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/democratic-republic-of-the-congo">Democratic Republic of the Congo</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/republic-of-the-congo">Republic of the Congo</a>. It is the home of the Yombe, a Kongo-speaking people known for their carved figures. Its forests supplied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timber">timber</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">ivory</a> and other goods to the coastal kingdoms.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mayombe.jpg" alt="Mayombe" width="320" height="642" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Origamiemensch · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Magische_Figur.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
